e of the USSR, GDR, and Czechoslovakia. Czechoslovakia was of note because at the 1st Athletics World Championships in 1983, " [:a {:href "/athletes/76554"} "Jarmila Kratochvílová"] " had won the 400/800 double, shortly after setting a world record of 1:53.28, which stood well into the 2020s. The final pace was set by Italy’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/71760"} "Gabriella Dorio"] " who led until 550 metres, when " [:a {:href "/athletes/75097"} "Doina Beşliu-Melinte"] " (ROM) took over. She was chased to the line by American " [:a {:href "/athletes/77838"} "Kim Gallagher"] " but never was caught. Dorio faded and the bronze medal went to Melinte’s teammate, " [:a {:href "/athletes/75128"} "Fiţa Lovin"] "."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "SF"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "315"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/75097"} "Doina Melinte"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/ROU"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/ROU.png"}] "ROU"]] [:td {} "2:02.77 (1 h3)"] [:td {} "2:01.42 (2 h1)"] [:td {} "1:57.60 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "377"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/77838"} "Kim Gallagher"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "2:00.37 (1 h4)"] [:td {} "2:00.48 (1 h1)"] [:td {} "1:58.63 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "314"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/75128"} "Fița Lovin"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/ROU"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; verti